<title>BELGIUM: Barco 1996 current profit up 31 pct.</title>
<headline>Barco 1996 current profit up 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current per share (francs) *    229  vs   201, up 14 pct</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)    *     62  vs    50, up 24 pct</p>
<p>    Group net profit		   2.37  vs  1.80, up 32 pct</p>
<p>    Net current profit		 2.80  vs  2.13, up 31 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Barco NV is a diversified Belgian electronics company whose main businesses are: projection and display systems; communication (cable and satellite) systems; automated and graphics systems. * Number of shares rose 15 percent to 12,203,840 in 1996 due to expiry of warrants.</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		     18.92  vs 15.08</p>
<p>    of which - visual systems	9.13  vs  6.85</p>
<p>    &quot;   &quot;    - communications	1.62  vs  1.00</p>
<p>    &quot;   &quot;    - automation	    3.41  vs  3.05</p>
<p>    &quot;   &quot;    - graphics		4.00  vs  3.51</p>
<p>    &quot;   &quot;    - other		   0.76  vs  0.66</p>
<p>Geographic breakdown of turnover (percent)</p>
<p>    Belgium				10.0  vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Western Europe		     46.0  vs  51.0</p>
<p>    Nafta				  26.0  vs  22.0</p>
<p>    Asia				   14.0  vs  12.0</p>
<p>    Other				   4.0  vs   4.0</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
